Berkeley DB 4.8.30.NC, vendored for Pinkcoin (Pink2)
====================================================

Origin:  db-4.8.30.NC.tar.gz
         https://download.oracle.com/berkeley-db/db-4.8.30.NC.tar.gz
         (mirror: https://gridcoin-depends-backup-sources.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/db-4.8.30.NC.tar.gz)
sha256:  12edc0df75bf9abd7f82f821795bcee50f42cb2e5f76a6a281b85732798364ef

Why 4.8: Pinkcoin wallets and block indexes are BDB 4.8 files, and every
2.4.0.0 release opens them with it. This tree is compiled from source so that
every platform build uses the same BDB. src/bdb48/CMakeLists.txt builds it with
its own configure under ExternalProject, as Gridcoin builds its bundled 5.3.
Configure flags: --enable-cxx --disable-shared --disable-replication, plus
--with-pic with ENABLE_PIE and --enable-mingw on Windows. No -DUNICODE or
-D_UNICODE on Windows: 2.4.0.0's BDB had neither, and Pink2 gives BDB narrow
paths in the ANSI code page.

Changes from the tarball (git history: two commits, the import and the rename)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removed directories, none of which configure or make reads for the static C++
library (the build is checked by building libdb_cxx.a natively and for MinGW):

  docs docs_src         documentation
  examples_c examples_cxx examples_java examples_csharp examples_stl
                        example programs
  java csharp libdb_java libdb_csharp
                        Java and C# bindings (configure is run without them)
  tcl                   Tcl API (needs --enable-tcl)
  perl php_db4 mod_db4  Perl, PHP and Apache bindings
  test test_micro test_stl
                        Tcl test suite and benchmarks, except test/include.tcl,
                        which dist/configure lists as an input file of
                        config.status
  build_brew build_s60 build_vxworks build_wince build_windows
                        project files for other build systems (MinGW builds
                        through dist/configure with --enable-mingw, and
                        os_windows is kept)
  os_brew os_qnx os_s60 os_vxworks
                        OS layers for platforms Pinkcoin does not build for

Kept although unused here: stl, db_sql, dist, and the command-line utilities
(db_dump and the others), which dist/Makefile.in expects.

Renames (whole words, in dbinc/atomic.h and mp/*.c, mutex/*.c): the
identifiers __atomic_compare_exchange and atomic_init collide with compiler
builtins in current GCC and Clang, so they are now __atomic_compare_exchange_db
and atomic_init_db. This is the recipe of .github/scripts/build-bdb48.sh in the
compat CI. Nothing else in the tree is modified.

Host triple: a native build passes no --host, and the 2009 config.guess and
config.sub need no update for arm64 macOS. config.guess names the processor
from `uname -p`, which there is "arm", and so reports arm-apple-darwin<release>,
a triple config.sub accepts; the macOS arm64 CI build configures BDB this way.
Only a cross build (CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING) passes --host, taken from
CMAKE_C_COMPILER_TARGET or else the compiler's -dumpmachine.
